{"id":"conditional-flow-matching-loss","t":"Conditional flow matching loss","tags":["Flow Matching","Generative Models","Loss Functions"],"d":"Medium","rt":"numpy","fn":"cfm_loss","tol":[1e-06,1e-08],"pkgs":[],"st":"Flow matching trains a velocity field $v_\\theta(x, t)$ whose ODE carries noise ($t = 0$) to data ($t = 1$). Like score matching, the marginal target is intractable, but a **conditional** target for one (noise, data) pair is easy. Use the straight-line path with a small minimum width $\\sigma_{\\min}$:\n\n$$x_t = \\big(1 - (1-\\sigma_{\\min})\\,t\\big)\\,x_0 + t\\,x_1, \\qquad u_t = \\frac{d x_t}{dt} = x_1 - (1-\\sigma_{\\min})\\,x_0$$\n\nand regress $v_\\theta(x_t, t)$ onto $u_t$ with mean squared error. Here $x_0$ is the noise sample and $x_1$ is the data sample.\n\nThe model is a toy linear field $v_\\theta(x, t) = x\\,W + t\\,c + b$.\n\nWrite `cfm_loss(x0, x1, t, W, c, b, sigma_min=0.0)` and return `(x_t, u_t, loss)`.\n\n## Inputs\n- `x0`: `(B, D)` noise; `x1`: `(B, D)` data; `t`: `(B,)` times in $[0, 1]$, one per pair.\n- `W`: `(D, D)` applied as `x @ W`; `c`, `b`: `(D,)`.\n\n## Output\n- `x_t`, `u_t`: `(B, D)` float arrays.\n- `loss`: Python `float`, the mean of $(v_\\theta(x_t, t) - u_t)^2$ over all $B\\times D$ entries.","starter":"import numpy as np\n\ndef cfm_loss(x0, x1, t, W, c, b, sigma_min=0.0):\n    \"\"\"Straight-path conditional flow matching. Return (x_t, u_t, loss).\"\"\"\n    raise NotImplementedError\n","hints":["Reshape `t` to `(B, 1)` so each pair gets its own time, then build $x_t$ by interpolating between noise and data.","Differentiate the path with respect to $t$: the target velocity $x_1 - (1-\\sigma_{\\min})x_0$ does not depend on $t$ at all.","The model output is `x_t @ W + t[:, None] * c + b`; the loss is `np.mean((v - u_t) ** 2)` over everything."],"sol":"import numpy as np\n\ndef cfm_loss(x0, x1, t, W, c, b, sigma_min=0.0):\n    x0, x1, W, c, b = (np.asarray(a, dtype=float) for a in (x0, x1, W, c, b))\n    tt = np.asarray(t, dtype=float)[:, None]               # (B, 1)\n    k = 1.0 - sigma_min\n    x_t = (1.0 - k * tt) * x0 + tt * x1\n    u_t = x1 - k * x0                                      # constant along the path, so no t\n    v = x_t @ W + tt * c + b\n    return x_t, u_t, float(np.mean((v - u_t) ** 2))\n","ex_md":"## Why it works\nEach pair defines a path whose marginal over pairs, $p_t(x)$, interpolates from the noise distribution to the data distribution. The marginal velocity that generates $p_t$ is the conditional velocity averaged over all pairs passing through $x$. Because MSE regression recovers a conditional expectation, minimising the conditional loss trains $v_\\theta$ to the marginal field, with gradients identical to the intractable marginal loss.\n\nWith $\\sigma_{\\min} = 0$ this is **rectified flow**: straight lines from noise to data, and target $x_1 - x_0$. A positive $\\sigma_{\\min}$ leaves the path a little noise at $t = 1$ (test 3: at $t = 1$, $x_t = \\sigma_{\\min}x_0 + x_1$).\n\n## Relation to diffusion\nA diffusion model with $\\varepsilon$-prediction is also a velocity field along a (curved) Gaussian path; flow matching just picks the path directly. Straighter paths need fewer ODE steps to sample.\n\n## Complexity\n$O(BD^2)$ for the model; the targets are $O(BD)$.\n\n## Common bugs\n- Swapping noise and data (here $t = 0$ is noise; some papers use the opposite convention).\n- Writing the target as $x_1 - x_t$ or $(x_1 - x_t)/(1-t)$: equal to $u_t$ only when $\\sigma_{\\min} = 0$, and the second divides by zero at $t = 1$.\n- Using one $t$ for the whole batch.\n\n## Interview follow-ups\n- How would you sample from the trained model? (Integrate $dx/dt = v_\\theta(x, t)$ from $t = 0$ to $1$ with Euler or Heun.)\n- What does minibatch optimal-transport pairing of $x_0$ and $x_1$ change, and why does it help?","nex":2,"shown":[{"in":"array([[1., 0.]])\narray([[3., 2.]])\narray([0.5])\narray([[0., 0.],\n       [0., 0.]])\narray([0., 0.])\narray([0., 0.])","out":"(array([[2., 1.]]), array([[2., 2.]]), 4.0)"},{"in":"array([[1.]])\narray([[2.]])\narray([0.])\narray([[0.]])\narray([0.])\narray([1.])","out":"(array([[1.]]), array([[1.]]), 0.0)"}],"lessons":[{"href":"../deep-learning/index.html#l07-06","t":"Score matching and flow matching","c":"Deep Learning"}],"related":["noise-prediction-loss","denoising-score-matching-loss","karras-euler-sampler"],"ntests":6,"tj":"[{\"a\": [{\"__nd__\": [[1.0, 0.0]], \"dtype\": \"float64\"}, {\"__nd__\": [[3.0, 2.0]], \"dtype\": \"float64\"}, {\"__nd__\": [0.5], \"dtype\": \"float64\"}, {\"__nd__\": [[0.0, 0.0], [0.0, 0.0]], \"dtype\": \"float64\"}, {\"__nd__\": [0.0, 0.0], \"dtype\": \"float64\"}, {\"__nd__\": [0.0, 0.0], \"dtype\": \"float64\"}], \"e\": {\"__tup__\": [{\"__nd__\": [[2.0, 1.0]], \"dtype\": \"float64\"}, {\"__nd__\": [[2.0, 2.0]], \"dtype\": \"float64\"}, 4.0]}}, {\"a\": [{\"__nd__\": [[1.0]], \"dtype\": \"float64\"}, {\"__nd__\": [[2.0]], \"dtype\": \"float64\"}, {\"__nd__\": [0.0], \"dtype\": \"float64\"}, {\"__nd__\": [[0.0]], \"dtype\": \"float64\"}, {\"__nd__\": [0.0], \"dtype\": \"float64\"}, {\"__nd__\": [1.0], \"dtype\": \"float64\"}], \"e\": {\"__tup__\": [{\"__nd__\": [[1.0]], \"dtype\": \"float64\"}, {\"__nd__\": [[1.0]], \"dtype\": \"float64\"}, 0.0]}}, {\"a\": [{\"__nd__\": [[2.0], [2.0]], \"dtype\": \"float64\"}, {\"__nd__\": [[0.0], [0.0]], \"dtype\": \"float64\"}, {\"__nd__\": [0.0, 1.0], \"dtype\": \"float64\"}, {\"__nd__\": [[0.0]], \"dtype\": \"float64\"}, {\"__nd__\": [0.0], \"dtype\": \"float64\"}, {\"__nd__\": [0.0], \"dtype\": \"float64\"}, 0.1], \"e\": {\"__tup__\": [{\"__nd__\": [[2.0], [0.19999999999999996]], \"dtype\": \"float64\"}, {\"__nd__\": [[-1.8], [-1.8]], \"dtype\": \"float64\"}, 3.24]}}, {\"a\": [{\"__nd__\": [[0.04872092360793993, 0.518163511364593, -0.11009940097747317], [-0.08903376282316156, 0.5025036488002448, 0.5105738622580861], [0.34507567321047217, -1.4208372310792416, -0.5697726964036604], [-0.3065754986173485, 0.73955397475